---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Espressif ESP-IDF and esp-zigbee-sdk
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Not vendored in git (fetched at build time into firmware/managed_components/,
which is gitignored). Apache License 2.0.
  https://github.com/espressif/esp-idf
  https://github.com/espressif/esp-zigbee-sdk

The Zigbee manufacturer code used in this project is 0x434E (see MANUFACTURER_ID.md).
It is this project's DIY code (ASCII "CN"), chosen from the quiet 0x3000–0x5FFF band.
It is not CSA-assigned and the device is not Zigbee-certified. Espressif's sample
default 0x131B is no longer used.

---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Good Display GDEY029T94 (SSD1680) init / partial-refresh sequences
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
firmware/components/display/ssd1680.c implements the panel driver. The init
and partial-refresh command sequences follow Good Display's GDEY029T94 sample
code and datasheet (not a verbatim copy of their sample tree). Confirm
redistribution terms against the PDF/sample package you used before shipping
products based on this driver.

---------------------------------------------------------------------------
LCSC / EasyEDA 3D STEP models
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
kicad/tstat.3dshapes/*.step (and .wrl) are mechanical models obtained from
LCSC / EasyEDA part pages for board preview and the case fit. They are
included for this hardware project; redistribution terms follow the vendor's
site terms. Replace or remove them if you need a stricter provenance chain.

